# Territory Forge (CR 607.2e, 607.5, 613.1f): with Panharmonicon out, Bot1's Forge enters on turn 3 and its "if you cast it"
# trigger triggers twice, exiling both of Bot2's Jeweled Amulets, so the Forge has the activated abilities of each. Bot1 pays
# {G} for the first Amulet's "{1}, {T}: Put a charge counter ... Note the type of mana spent" (the Forge's second ability, after
# its own trigger). On turn 5 Bot1 taps the Forge for the second Amulet's "{T}, Remove a charge counter: Add one mana of this
# artifact's last noted type" (its fifth). The two Amulets' abilities are two lendings, each linked only to its own (CR 607.5): the
# second Amulet's noting ability noted nothing, so the counter is removed and no mana is added.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Panharmonicon
Territory Forge
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Jeweled Amulet x2
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
